  "correctValue": null,
  "solution": {
    "text": "<blockquote><p>According to the question, In the first step of the reaction, when cyclo-pentyl-chloride reacts with magnesium in the presence of dry ether than cyclo-pentyl-magnesium-chloride (grignard reagent) is formed.&nbsp;</p><p>In the second step of the reaction, when grignard reagent is react with a compound, which has active hydrogen than grignard reagent abstract hydrogen from&nbsp;active hydrogen compound and converted in to alkane.&nbsp;</p><p>So cyclo-pentane is formed as the product(second step of the reaction) of this reaction.&nbsp;</p><p><img src=\"https://cdn-question-pool.getmarks.app/pyq/jee_main/3945a8a7-cdad-4dd7-956f-53ce630b91f6-image.png\" style=\"width: 576px; height: 94px;\" /></p></blockquote>",
